Libraries tools/patch-live.py copies into push3_opt/push3/lib/xkbcommon. The
shim (standalone.cpp, loadXkbcommon) loads them only when the system has no
libxkbcommon-x11; otherwise the system's own pair is used.

libxkbcommon.so.0, libxkbcommon-x11.so.0: xkbcommon 1.5.0 from Debian 12
(packages libxkbcommon0 and libxkbcommon-x11-0 1.5.0-1 from deb.debian.org
over HTTPS, matching the SHA256 in bookworm's Packages index:
e3fe045b9a33a101de1c5a912a4a10928db055c3f68930f47eccbb44d7c7d54e and
9b34d760f0ca0f125419a6becc6492c489f0371953ef42caad3401199a497ff5).
libxkbcommon-x11 builds keymaps with libxkbcommon's internal structures, so the
two must be the same version: Arch's x11 part (1.13) with Ubuntu's libxkbcommon
(1.6) crashed Live on the first key press. These need glibc 2.33, below Live's
own 2.35; Arch's and Ubuntu 24.04's builds need 2.38 (for __isoc23_strtol).

innoextract: innoextract 1.10-dev (git 6e9e34e, github.com/dscharrer/innoextract,
zlib licence, LICENSE.innoextract), for install.sh. Live 12.4's Windows installer is Inno Setup 6.4
(setup data version 6.4.0.1), which innoextract 1.9, the release most
distributions ship (Ubuntu, Mint, Debian, Fedora), cannot read. Boost,
libstdc++ and libgcc are linked in; it needs glibc 2.35, liblzma.so.5,
libz.so.1 and libbz2.so.1.0 (install.sh links libbz2.so.1 under that name on
Fedora and openSUSE). Built with Arch's Boost 1.92 static libraries and the
AUR package's boost1.89.0.patch:
  g++ -O2 -c ../innoextract-compat.cpp -o ic.o
  g++ -O2 -c ../../shim/glibccompat.cpp -o gc.o   (wic_unpacked/shim)
  cmake <src> -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DUSE_STATIC_LIBS=OFF -DBoost_USE_STATIC_LIBS=ON \
      -DUSE_LTO=OFF -DBUILD_TESTS=OFF \
      -DCMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS="$PWD/ic.o $PWD/gc.o -static-libstdc++ -static-libgcc -Wl,--as-needed -s"
  make
(innoextract-compat.cpp: arc4random, GLIBC_2.36 in Arch's static Boost.Random;
glibccompat.cpp: the C23 strtoul and sscanf of glibc 2.38 headers.)
